{
  "editions": [
    {
      "edition": "standard",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "τούτοις οὖν ἐστὶ μετάνοια, ἐὰν ταχὺ μετανοήσωσι καὶ μὴ ἐπιμείνωσι ταῖς ἡδοναῖς αὐτῶν·",
          "english_quote": "Retain each rod group, response conditions, renewed seal and plural spirits; select sinners with declared Athos and partial Michigan evidence.",
          "issue": "The unit-specific theological metadata claims decisions concerning a renewed seal, plural spirits, and a sinners reading, none of which occurs in the selected section. The supplied comparison report locates the sinners selection in S.8.vi.6, not S.8.viii. This misattributes decisions from other sections to this translation.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace this metadata with a decision scoped to S.8.viii: retain its distinct rod groups, conditional repentance, and death warnings, and retain the working proportions in viii.4 with the reported Athos alternative disclosed. Keep decisions about the seal, spirits, and sinners in their applicable units.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "Οἱ δὲ ἐπιδεδωκότες τὰς ῥάβδους ἥμισυ μὲν χλωράς, ἥμισυ δὲ ξηράς,",
          "english_quote": "The people whose rods were half green and half dry",
          "issue": "The simplified text omits the act of handing in the rods. The source identifies this group by the rods they submitted, not merely by possessing rods of these colors.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use wording such as: “The people who handed in rods that were half green and half dry”.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "οἱ δὲ τὰ δύο μέρη χλωρά, τὸ δὲ τρίτον ξηρὸν ἐπιδεδωκότες,",
          "english_quote": "The people whose rods were two-thirds green and one-third dry",
          "issue": "The second rod-group description independently drops the source's act of handing in the rods.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use wording such as: “The people who handed in rods that were two-thirds green and one-third dry”. Retain the disclosed working proportions.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τούτοις οὖν ἐστὶ μετάνοια, ἐὰν ταχὺ μετανοήσωσι καὶ μὴ ἐπιμείνωσι ταῖς ἡδοναῖς αὐτῶν·",
          "english_quote": "These still have an opportunity to repent. They must repent quickly and stop pursuing their pleasures.",
          "issue": "The source makes the availability of repentance conditional on repenting quickly and not persisting in their pleasures. The simplified version first asserts the opportunity without qualification, then turns the conditions into a separate obligation. This weakens the explicit conditional relationship, notwithstanding the footnote's claim that the conditions remain explicit.",
          "suggested_revision": "Restore the conditional connection, for example: “These have an opportunity to repent if they repent quickly and do not keep pursuing their pleasures.” If “still” is retained as a disclosed editorial rendering, keep that disclosure distinct from the selected Greek wording.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τούτοις οὖν ἐστὶ μετάνοια, ἐὰν ταχὺ μετανοήσωσι καὶ μὴ ἐπιμείνωσι ταῖς ἡδοναῖς αὐτῶν·",
          "english_quote": "Retain each rod group, response conditions, renewed seal and plural spirits; select sinners with declared Athos and partial Michigan evidence.",
          "issue": "The theological metadata attributes a renewed seal, plural spirits, and a sinners selection to this section, although they are absent from its selected source. The supplied evidence places the sinners decision in S.8.vi.6. The simplification metadata likewise claims preservation of these absent elements.",
          "suggested_revision": "Scope both metadata blocks to the actual contents of S.8.viii: its rod groups, repentance conditions, warnings, and disclosed proportion alternative. Remove the seal, spirits, and sinners claims from this unit's metadata.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The standard translation covers the selected clauses faithfully but needs correction of mis-scoped metadata. The simplified edition additionally omits both rod-submission actions and weakens the explicit condition governing repentance in paragraph 5. The disclosed working color proportions should be retained rather than replaced merely because an Athos alternative is reported. Witness disclosures were assessed against the supplied project reports, not authenticated against unseen manuscripts. Suggested corrections require fresh review."
}
